-- a citation inside written text: the words shown, and the definition they refer to. The reference is the
-- definition's own identifier in the citing code, so the checker resolves it (a citation of nothing does
-- not check) and the store records it among the citing definition's dependencies (deps/), whose reverse
-- (users/, `hyperactive def`'s "used by") is every citation of it: the link and its backlink are what
-- the store already keeps, not a string spelling a target (paper §10.8: a reference refers to the
-- definition, a name is a view of it). Every projection of the text shows the words; a view that draws
-- links (an HTML page of the knowledge graph) reads the reference from the code and the store.
cite : {A : Type} → A → List Word → List Word
cite a w = w
